import VersoManual
import Companion.Source
import Companion.Safrole
import Companion.PVM

open Verso.Genre Manual
open Companion

set_option pp.rawOnError true

#doc (Manual) "A Companion to the Gray Paper" =>
%%%
authors := ["jam-lean"]
shortTitle := "GP companion"
%%%

This book reads the [Gray Paper](https://graypaper.com) v0.8.1 alongside
[jam-lean](https://github.com/ascrivener/jam-lean), a Lean 4 model of JAM. For each part of the
paper it shows:

* the paper's equations, as they are written in the paper;
* the Lean definitions that implement them, read from the model's source when the book is built
  (so they are never out of date with the code);
* the readings the model chose where the paper is ambiguous, with links to the model's list of
  [upstream candidates](https://github.com/ascrivener/jam-lean/blob/main/docs/upstream-candidates.md);
* the theorems proved about those definitions, with their exact statements.

Names in `this style` link to the [API reference](/jam-lean/api/), generated by doc-gen4, where
every definition and theorem of `PVM`, `JAM` and `JamCrypto` is listed with its docstring.

The book is built with Verso. If a definition it quotes is renamed or removed, or a theorem's
statement no longer elaborates, the book fails to build. That is how it stays in step with the
model.

# Roadmap
%%%
tag := "roadmap"
%%%

Chapters follow the order of the paper's sections. Two are written so far; the others are listed
with the model modules that implement them.

* §4–§5 The state, the header and the block: `JAM/State.lean`, `JAM/Block.lean`, `JAM/BlockImport.lean`
* *§6 Safrole* ({ref "safrole"}[written]): `JAM/Safrole.lean`
* §7 Recent history: `JAM/History.lean`
* §8 Authorization: `JAM/Authorization.lean`
* §9 Service accounts: `JAM/Account.lean`
* §10 Disputes: `JAM/Disputes.lean`
* §11 Reports and assurances: `JAM/Reports.lean`, `JAM/Assurances.lean`, `JAM/Guarantee.lean`
* §12 Accumulation and preimages: `JAM/Accumulate.lean`, `JAM/Accumulation.lean`, `JAM/Preimages.lean`
* §13 Statistics: `JAM/Statistics.lean`
* §14 Work packages and refinement: `JAM/Work.lean`, `JAM/Refine.lean`, `JAM/Segments.lean`
* §17 Auditing: `JAM/Auditing.lean`
* *Appendix A, the PVM* ({ref "pvm"}[written]): `PVM/Machine.lean`, `PVM/Exec.lean`, `PVM/Gas.lean`, `PVM/Memory.lean`
* Appendix B, PVM invocations: `PVM/Invocation.lean`, `JAM/Host/`
* Appendix C–D, serialization and Merklization: `JAM/Codec.lean`, `JAM/Merkle.lean`, `JAM/Trie.lean`
* Appendix G–H, cryptography and erasure coding: `JAM/Crypto.lean` and `JamCrypto/`, `JAM/Erasure.lean`

{include 1 Companion.Safrole}

{include 1 Companion.PVM}
